      "writtenOn": "2019-04-17T21:26:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You would expect an encoding of a MAC state to only allow generating outputs for inputs with that prefix, but that is not the case and would be surprising. With HMAC, it allows generating outputs for any inputs. KMAC is better, but any buffered uncompressed input could still be rolled back. (Right?)\n\nSo yeah, I feel like it\u0027s too subtle, let\u0027s not.",
